{
 "id": "ll_lanterns",
 "title": "Lanterns in the Fen",
 "kind": "hero",
 "seed": 4303,
 "intro": [
  "South of the barrows the land gives up and goes to water. The fen road runs on boards and old causeways through the reeds, past Stilt Market and drowned Brackwater, to Fenlight, a lantern-town that has kept a light burning against the marsh for three hundred years.",
  "The light still burns. It burns green now. The Hollow hold Fenlight, and the man who holds it for them was a lantern-priest once: Father Corvin Mire. His lanterns hang along the fen road, and wherever they shine the dead climb out of the mud.",
  "Sister Edda Vey of the lantern temples is waiting at the Lantern House north of the crossing. She knew Corvin. Find her, put out his lanterns, and take Fenlight."
 ],
 "outro": [
  {
   "if": {
    "all": [
     {
      "flag": "edda_joined"
     },
     {
      "flag": "heard_leak"
     }
    ]
   },
   "text": [
    "Fenlight's lantern burns yellow again by nightfall. Edda sits up with Corvin's lamp in her lap and reads the ash in it the way the temples taught them both.",
    "She goes pale. \"He was right about one thing,\" she says. \"It isn't something waking.\" She tips the ash into the water and watches it sink. \"Something is leaking.\""
   ]
  },
  {
   "if": {
    "flag": "edda_joined"
   },
   "text": [
    "Fenlight's lantern burns yellow again by nightfall. Edda sits up with Corvin's lamp in her lap and reads the ash in it the way the temples taught them both.",
    "\"Not something waking,\" she says at last, very quietly. \"Something leaking. And we are standing on the lid.\""
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": [
    "Fenlight's lantern burns yellow again by nightfall. A rider takes Corvin's lamp north to the Lantern House, as Sister Edda asked.",
    "Her answer comes back two days later, in a hand that shakes: \"Not something waking. Something leaking. Come back to the Lantern House before you go any further south.\""
   ]
  }
 ],
