 "dialogues": {
  "edda_meet": {
   "nodes": {
    "start": {
     "text": "Sir Aldous. I've watched the fen road for three nights from this porch. Every night another lantern is lit, and every lantern is one of ours.",
     "next": "b"
    },
    "b": {
     "who": "hero",
     "text": "Yours?",
     "next": "c"
    },
    "c": {
     "text": "The temples' lanterns. The blue flame burns near the dead to warn the living. Corvin has turned them green, so they call the dead instead. He was my teacher. He taught me to light them.",
     "next": "d"
    },
    "d": {
     "text": "Feel the boards under you. They're warm. The temples say the ground is waking, my lord. I think it's worse than that. Let me walk with you and I'll show you.",
     "choices": [
      {
       "text": "Then walk with us, sister. We'll need your lamp.",
       "do": [
        {
         "flag": "edda_met"
        },
        {
         "flag": "edda_joined"
        },
        {
         "join": "edda"
        }
       ],
       "next": "join"
      },
      {
       "text": "Stay with the temple. If we fall, someone has to warn Highmere.",
       "do": [
        {
         "flag": "edda_met"
        },
        {
         "flag": "edda_stays"
        }
       ],
       "next": "stay"
      }
     ]
    },
    "join": {
     "text": "Then put the lanterns out one by one, and keep me close when we reach Fenlight. I want to speak to him before you kill him."
    },
    "stay": {
     "text": "As you say. Take the temple's blessing, then: the little shrine by the reeds keeps it. And if you find Corvin... bring me his lamp.",
     "do": [
      {
       "potion": "mana",
       "n": 2
      }
     ]
    }
   }
  },
  "edda_stays": {
   "nodes": {
    "start": {
     "text": "The lamp burns blue tonight, my lord. The dead are close. Keep to the boards."
    }
   }
  },
  "jory_ask": {
   "nodes": {
    "start": {
     "who": "jory",
     "text": "A knight! Do knights eat eels? Never mind. My lord, something big lives in the south reeds now. Took two boats and the men in them.",
     "next": "b"
    },
    "b": {
     "text": "Since the green lights came the bog lurkers come up from the deep pools. Kill them, and Stilt Market will remember it.",
     "choices": [
      {
       "text": "I'll deal with them.",
       "do": [
        {
         "start_quest": "eels"
        }
       ]
      },
      {
       "text": "The dead first. Then your eels."
      }
     ]
    }
   }
  },
  "jory_back": {
   "nodes": {
    "start": {
     "text": "Gone? Both of them? Gods, my lord, I'll put your name on a boat. What does the market owe you?",
     "choices": [
      {
       "text": "Nothing. Feed the Brackwater folk who come in.",
       "do": [
        {
         "flag": "jory_done"
        },
        {
         "flag": "jory_free"
        },
        {
         "potion": "health",
         "n": 2
        }
       ],
       "next": "free"
      },
      {
       "text": "You promised a reward. I'll take it.",
       "do": [
        {
         "flag": "jory_done"
        },
        {
         "flag": "jory_paid"
        },
        {
         "marks": 90
        }
       ],
       "next": "paid"
      }
     ]
    },
    "free": {
     "text": "A knight who works for eels and soup. Take these, at least. My wife brews them, they taste of bog."
    },
    "paid": {
     "text": "Fair's fair. Ninety marks, my lord. That's a season of eels."
    }
   }
  },
  "jory_idle": {
   "nodes": {
    "start": {
     "text": "Boats are going out again. Slowly."
    }
   }
  },
  "ama_ask": {
   "nodes": {
    "start": {
     "text": "My lord Wren. You took us in at Waymeet. Now I'm asking for more. The rest of Brackwater was walked south, into the fen. Some of them may still be breathing.",
     "next": "b"
    },
    "b": {
     "text": "The old drowned chapel past the village. That's where the green light was. Please.",
     "choices": [
      {
       "text": "I'll find them.",
       "do": [
        {
         "start_quest": "walked"
        }
       ]
      },
      {
       "text": "I can't promise you anything, Ama.",
       "do": [
        {
         "start_quest": "walked"
        }
       ],
       "next": "c"
      }
     ]
    },
    "c": {
     "text": "I know. Look anyway."
    }
   }
  },
  "ama_back": {
   "nodes": {
    "start": {
     "text": "You went. You actually went. Tell me, my lord.",
     "next": "tell"
    },
    "tell": {
     "who": "hero",
     "text": "I'll tell you everything, Ama. Sit down.",
     "do": [
      {
       "flag": "walked_told"
      }
     ]
    }
   }
  },
  "ama_idle": {
   "nodes": {
    "start": {
     "text": "Greyhold feeds us. We won't forget it."
    }
   }
  },
  "hester_ask": {
   "nodes": {
    "start": {
     "text": "You're the knight from Greyhold? I'm Hester, from Brackwater. What's left of it. I hid in the eel traps when they came.",
     "next": "b"
    },
    "b": {
     "text": "They walked everyone south to the drowned chapel. In rows, singing. My father was singing. Please, my lord.",
     "choices": [
      {
       "text": "I'll go to the chapel.",
       "do": [
        {
         "start_quest": "walked"
        }
       ]
      },
      {
       "text": "If they were singing, Hester, they're gone.",
       "do": [
        {
         "start_quest": "walked"
        }
       ],
       "next": "c"
      }
     ]
    },
    "c": {
     "text": "Then go and make sure. I can't."
    }
   }
  },
  "hester_back": {
   "nodes": {
    "start": {
     "text": "My lord? Did you... was my father there?",
     "next": "tell"
    },
    "tell": {
     "who": "hero",
     "text": "He was there, Hester. Listen.",
     "do": [
      {
       "flag": "walked_told"
      }
     ]
    }
   }
  },
  "hester_idle": {
   "nodes": {
    "start": {
     "text": "I'm learning to sell eels. Jory says I'm terrible at it."
    }
   }
